# Environment variable template for the acceleration-report analysis pipeline.
# See AAP §0.6.2.
#
# Usage:
#     cp .env.example .env
#     # Fill in real values for any optional variables you want to provide.
#     # All variables are optional; the pipeline degrades gracefully when each
#     # is absent (confidence tiers drop and Insufficient-Signal markers appear
#     # for the affected metrics).
#
# Secrets MUST NOT be committed. .env is git-ignored by .gitignore in this
# workspace.

# -------- Required for repository identification --------
# GitHub owner/repository slug for the analyzed repository.
# Defaults to the value derived from `git remote get-url origin` when absent.
GITHUB_REPO_SLUG=Blitzy-Sandbox/blitzy-RudderStack

# -------- Optional: GitHub API access --------
# A GitHub personal access token (classic) or fine-grained token with `repo`
# read scope. Increases the unauthenticated rate limit (60 req/hr -> 5000 req/hr)
# and is required for any private-repo Releases / Actions / branches/protection
# endpoint. Leave unset to run in offline / local-git fallback mode.
# GH_TOKEN=ghp_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# -------- Optional: Linear API access --------
# A Linear API key. Required only for Metric 6 (Flow Distribution by issue
# label) and Metric 12 (Defects Out of SLA). When absent, both metrics fall back
# to in-repo signals; Metric 12 reports "Insufficient signal — no SLA source"
# unless a SLA policy document is discovered in the repository tree.
# LINEAR_API_KEY=lin_api_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# -------- Optional: analysis window override --------
# Override the auto-detected analysis window. The pipeline auto-detects the
# inflection point and the window endpoints; these variables let you pin them
# for a re-run. ISO-8601 UTC dates.
# ANALYSIS_START_DATE=2025-09-01
# ANALYSIS_END_DATE=2026-05-23

# -------- Internal: per-run correlation ID --------
# Set by scripts/00_environment.sh. Do not set manually unless you are
# explicitly correlating a re-run with a prior run's logs.
# BLITZY_RUN_ID=
